---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { analytics } from '../config/analytics';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
import { withBasePath } from '../lib/urls';
const homeURL = withBasePath('/', import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
const linkedIn = profile.contact.links.find((link) =>
  ['linkedin.com', 'www.linkedin.com'].includes(new URL(link.url).hostname),
);
---

<SiteLayout
  title={`Privacy policy | FOLIO`}
  description="How FOLIO handles contact details, optional analytics and privacy choices."
>
  <article class="privacy-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <a class="text-link" href={homeURL}>
      ← Back to FOLIO
    </a>
    <p class="eyebrow">Your privacy</p>
    <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: 23 October 2026</p>
    <p>
      FOLIO is the professional portfolio of {profile.identity.name}. It is a
      static website with no accounts, contact form, payments or embedded social
      media. You can browse the portfolio and contact me without accepting
      optional analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact and personal information</h2>
    <p>
      {profile.identity.name} is responsible for the use of personal information
      in connection with this portfolio.{' '}
      {profile.contact.email ? (
        <>
          For privacy requests, contact{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${profile.contact.email}`}>
            {profile.contact.email}
          </a>
          .
        </>
      ) : linkedIn ? (
        <>
          For privacy requests, contact me through my{' '}
          <a href={linkedIn.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            LinkedIn profile (opens in a new tab)
          </a>
          .
        </>
      ) : (
        <>Contact details are currently unavailable.</>
      )}{' '}
      An email link opens your own email application. LinkedIn and CV links open
      LinkedIn; its privacy terms apply when you leave this website.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you contact me, I use the information you choose to provide to respond
      and discuss professional opportunities. Correspondence is kept only as
      needed for that purpose and applicable legal obligations. Please avoid
      sending unnecessary sensitive information.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and essential features</h2>
    <p>
      This site is served by GitHub Pages. The hosting provider processes
      technical requests needed to deliver and protect the website, which can
      include an IP address and request information. See the{' '}
      <a
        href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        GitHub privacy statement (opens in a new tab)
      </a>
      . Fonts and site images are served with the website, without external font
      requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Microsoft Clarity</h2>
    <p class="privacy-state">
      {analytics.enabled
        ? 'Optional analytics is configured. Clarity starts only after you accept analytics.'
        : 'Optional analytics is currently disabled. This version does not load Microsoft Clarity.'}
    </p>
    <p>
      When enabled and accepted, Microsoft Clarity processes interaction and
      technical usage data to help improve this portfolio, including heatmaps
      and session replay. This may include browser and device information, page
      visits, clicks and scrolling. Automatic usage data can include page and
      clicked-link URLs and referrer information. Text content is masked. FOLIO
      sends only fixed action names for CV, LinkedIn, email and selected
      navigation actions; custom events do not contain names, email addresses,
      message text or URLs. No custom visitor identifiers are sent. Advertising
      storage consent is always denied.
    </p>
    <p>
      Clarity may use first-party cookies such as <code>_clck</code> and
      <code>_clsk</code> to recognise a browser and connect page views.
      Microsoft describes its processing, applicable retention periods,
      potential international transfers and privacy choices in the{' '}
      <a
        href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/en-us/privacystatement"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Microsoft privacy statement (opens in a new tab)
      </a>{' '}
      and{' '}
      <a
        href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/clarity/setup-and-installation/clarity-cookies"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Clarity cookie documentation (opens in a new tab)
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>Your choice and withdrawal</h2>
    <p>
      Optional analytics relies on your consent. Accept and Reject are equally
      available. Before acceptance, and after rejection, this website does not
      load the Clarity script or send optional analytics events. Your decision
      is stored locally in your browser as <code>folio.consent.v1</code> for up
      to 180 days; it contains only the choice, policy version, project
      reference and decision time. If storage is unavailable, the choice applies
      to the current page only. A changed analytics project or expired decision
      requires a fresh choice. If browser storage cannot be updated, a temporary
      URL flag keeps rejection effective while you navigate this website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Open Privacy preferences in the footer at any time to change or withdraw
      consent. Rejection removes this site's accessible Clarity cookies. If an
      analytics session has started, the page refreshes to stop it completely.
      This does not erase data already received by Microsoft or cookies on
      another domain; use Microsoft's privacy controls or contact me about
      applicable deletion rights. All core features remain available.
    </p>
    <button
      class="button button--secondary"
      type="button"
      data-consent-open
      hidden
    >
      Privacy preferences
    </button>
    <noscript>
      <p>
        JavaScript is disabled, so optional analytics cannot run. No consent
        action is needed.
      </p>
    </noscript>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on applicable law, you may request access, correction, deletion,
      restriction or portability of your personal information, object to certain
      processing, withdraw consent and complain to a competent data protection
      authority. Contact me using the email above. Withdrawing consent does not
      affect processing that was lawful before withdrawal.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    max-width: var(--content-narrow);
    margin: var(--space-6) auto var(--space-12);
    padding: var(--section-padding);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-section);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }
  .privacy-page .eyebrow {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
  }
  .privacy-page h1 {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .privacy-page h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .privacy-page p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-block: var(--space-4);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .privacy-page a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
  .privacy-page .privacy-updated {
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .privacy-page .privacy-state {
    padding: var(--space-4);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background: var(--color-background-secondary);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }
  .privacy-page code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
